@rudolfix, thanks! The docs update is sufficient, with two notes from running this at scale:

- `clickhouse_adapter(partition="_dlt_load_id")` partitions the final table as well. Staging and final need different partition keys, so that part belongs in the subclass.
- With `truncate_staging_dataset_before_load=false`, nothing removes finished loads from a shared staging table, and `truncate_staging_dataset=true` at the end of a load truncates other pipelines’ in-flight rows. Worth a caution next to the new setting: the subclass has to own the cleanup, for ClickHouse `DROP PARTITION` on the load id.
